diff --git a/changelog/+xpbd-joint-coloring-7c3d9e21.added.md b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-coloring-7c3d9e21.added.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2a387c13a863c70a6a5a94092a425f6e3bf02098
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-coloring-7c3d9e21.added.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Add `SolverXPBD(joint_coloring=True)` to solve joints Gauss-Seidel by color (no two joints of a color share a body) instead of summing all joint corrections per body, and `joint_extra_iterations` for joint-only passes after the main iterations. On a 44-body humanoid at 4 iterations / 1.25 ms, coloring with relaxation 0.8 reduces the joint-anchor drift from 14.8 mm to 3.4 mm (median).
diff --git a/changelog/+xpbd-joint-drives-5b2e8d14.changed.md b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-drives-5b2e8d14.changed.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8bcb857168273801e03f3de8b034e2421cf819ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-drives-5b2e8d14.changed.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Change `SolverXPBD` joint drives to `joint_drive_mode="pd"`: the PD law of the state at the start of the step (damping backward-Euler on its own effect), bounded by `Model.joint_effort_limit`, so `joint_target_ke`/`joint_target_kd` are the stiffness and damping at any iteration count (the former compliance drive, still available as `joint_drive_mode="compliance"`, had an effective stiffness of 72-1240 N m/rad for `ke` 200 over 1-16 iterations). `joint_drive_mode="implicit"` solves the drive as implicit PD rows with accumulated impulses.
diff --git a/changelog/+xpbd-joint-relaxation-5b2e8d14.fixed.md b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-relaxation-5b2e8d14.fixed.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b6175bb530641a2670c2cb805a51316fc60dc68e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/+xpbd-joint-relaxation-5b2e8d14.fixed.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Fix `SolverXPBD` positional joint rows scaling the moment of their impulse by `joint_angular_relaxation` instead of `joint_linear_relaxation`, which made a pendulum respond 43 % too fast to a joint torque and 18 % too slowly to gravity at the defaults. The default `joint_linear_relaxation` is now 0.5 (0.7 injects energy into a floating humanoid with consistent rows); pass `joint_legacy_relaxation=True` for the former behaviour.
